{
  "gaps": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "status": "unproved",
      "reason": "The two cyclotomic class requirements are incompatible as written. Every member of S is selected from places of class 1 modulo M, but its required class of −1 modulo M3^c reduces to −1 modulo M. Since M is a positive multiple of 18480, these residues are distinct. Thus S is empty, contradicting H ≥ T/log b > 0. If the two requirements concern different class maps, the sketch needs to define those maps."
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "status": "incomplete",
      "reason": "The target space, its integral structure, the theta lift maps, and the formula for their main height are unspecified, so there is no way to check the covolume or index estimates or identify the height remainder with Q_u. The stated count has a conditional elementary proof. If the tops occur once per unit class above 1 modulo M, S consists of classes above −1, and ν is a unit modulo M3^c2^s, then multiplication by −ν maps the top fiber bijectively onto the fiber above −ν modulo M. Its image meets S in exactly H classes when ν ≡ 1 modulo M and in zero classes otherwise. Even that count does not establish the weighted prime-sum identity without a height formula."
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "status": "incomplete",
      "reason": "The rank-one and good-lift denominator bounds and the local estimates relating them to the determinant are unspecified. There is also an algebraic error in the stated cancellation. The product of Z(ϑ_ι)/Z(1) and Z(1)^2/Z(ϑ_ι)^2 is Z(1)/Z(ϑ_ι), and equality of the two determinants has not been established. The product formula for a nonzero algebraic number concerns its absolute values over all places and does not give the claimed inequality without the missing local estimates."
    }
  ],
  "parent_closes": false,
  "parent_reason": "The tower requirements conflict as written, and neither covolume bound has been established. The final algebra is valid conditional on those bounds. With A = h − mQ_u + L, subtracting DA from the claimed comparison gives mQ_u ≤ 4L + ((D − n)/D)(−A) + 2δ/D, which yields the stated bound using the three estimates from Gap 2. The last numerical estimate also follows if ‘near xb’ supplies a ≥ Cxb for some fixed C > 0. Writing t = log b = x^ε, the right side is at most 34tB + 4x^99 for large x, and B ≥ Cx exp(t)t^3. Dividing by t²B gives a quantity tending to zero for each fixed ε > 0. This estimate is independent of u, but the construction of common data and the covolume comparisons for every u remain unresolved."
}
